VERDICT
  The M = 2F-1 disagreeing set is exactly the pairs whose exact product is
  congruent to 2^(F-1) - 1 modulo 2^F: the products sitting one unit below the
  F-level tie, which the single dropped bit rounds up ONTO the tie, where
  ties-to-even then breaks the other way. The count is the number of such
  products, which is 2^(F-1).
